  "title": "Metrics and Monitoring",
  "description": "Collect metrics with Prometheus and visualize with Grafana.",
  "order": 4,
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedMinutes": 17,
  "tags": ["metrics", "prometheus", "grafana"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Metrics are numeric values aggregated over time. Prometheus collects metrics; Grafana visualizes them."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "Metric",
            "definition": "A numeric value aggregated over time."
          },
          {
            "term": "Prometheus",
            "definition": "A metrics collection and query system."
          },
          {
            "term": "Grafana",
            "definition": "A visualization and dashboard tool."
          },
          {
            "term": "Counter",
            "definition": "A metric that only increases (e.g., request count)."
          },
          {
            "term": "Histogram",
            "definition": "A metric that samples observations into buckets."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Metric Types"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Type", "Description", "Example"],
        "rows": [
          ["Counter", "Monotonically increasing", "Request count, error count"],
          ["Gauge", "Value that can go up/down", "Memory usage, queue depth"],
          ["Histogram", "Distribution in buckets", "Request latency"],
          ["Summary", "Distribution with quantiles", "Latency percentiles"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "RED Method"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "For each service, track: Rate (requests/sec), Errors (error rate), Duration (latency percentiles). These three metrics capture service health."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "USE Method"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "For each resource, track: Utilization (how busy), Saturation (queue depth), Errors (resource errors). Useful for infrastructure."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Prometheus + Grafana"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Prometheus scrapes metrics endpoints. It stores time-series data and provides PromQL for querying. Grafana connects to Prometheus to build dashboards and alerts."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
